The registry's agent-skills lintSuppressions array is a line-numbered mirror of these three .eta templates' front-config lintSuppressions blocks, which the compiler actually reads to suppress lint at build time; registry-reconciliation.test.ts checks only the aggregate count against lintSuppressionBudget, so a rule-name or line-range edit in one place that isn't mirrored in the other passes every test while becoming false documentation. Same pattern as voice-lint-suppression-anchors, applied to the agent-skills plugin's own suppressions (including the reference/helper-reference.md.eta ranges that plugins/agent-skills/scripts/sync-helper-reference.mjs regenerates). template-authoring/SKILL.md.eta no longer anchors this span: its one suppression was removed after the underlying cross-dialect skill reference was fixed rather than suppressed, so it carries no front-config lintSuppressions block to mirror.
